       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen is 5 times the maximum daily dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it carries a high risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, kidney failure, and metabolic acidosis. You also gave no clinical reason for it, so I can't treat it as intentional dosing.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** Tell me the dose and frequency, for example 800 mg PO four times daily (3200 mg/day). I can enter it immediately.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual reason for a higher dose, a pharmacist or the attending can review it. The order can go in through whatever override process your hospital uses.\n- **Check for a unit or typo error.** Sometimes \"4000\" is a slip for \"400,\" which would be 400 mg PO four times daily.\n\nIf you want to treat a specific problem, such as pain, fever, or inflammation, tell me which one. I can help you pick a regimen."
      }
